A big (but useful) refactor will be migrating from podman compose to quadlets.
As part of this migration, we should also switch to using rootless podman.

This will add a lot of complexity in our configuration, so we will additionally
need to migrate this stack to ansible. We want ansible anyway for configuring
firewalld.

We have the following containers
- jellyfin
- gluetun
- tinymediamanager
- slskd
- transmission
- syncthing

jellyfin should be running rootless under podman.

gluetun, slskd, and transmission should be running rootless under podman.
These also need to run together - they need the gluetun network.
gluetun also needs to manipulate slskd's volume to pass the forwarded port.
I think this is best done with kube yaml instead of quadlets.

tinymediamanager should be running rootless under k9.
syncthing should be running rootless under k9.

Also for references, these are our volumes. These are prefixed with `mimir`
because that was the pod name. I think this will probably be updated to be
prefixed with the user, so `podman` or `k9`.
```
DRIVER      VOLUME NAME
local       mimir_jellyfin_config
local       mimir_jellyfin_cache
local       mimir_slskd_app
local       mimir_syncthing_config
local       mimir_tinymediamanager_data
local       mimir_transmission_config
```

Also all our services should be cleaned up with healthchecks, etc.

- Use tailscale ACL as source of truth for firewall configuration
  - This saves having to configure both tailscale and firewalld
  - We'll want to setup ansible with the ACL so we can version control this
- Syncthing between mimir/helios/thinkpad
  - Music is setup
  - Right now I have my books in ~/Documents. This definitely becomes problematic with syncthing.
    - Best to just move ~/Documents/Books to ~/Books I think.
  - Games should be setup for urdr
  - Videos... should be setup, but it's not happening for a while :(.
- Automated backups with rclone (especially for podman volumes)
